  "question": {
    "text": "A point <math><mi>P</mi></math> on the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the foot of the perpendicular from it upon the directrix and the focus are the vertices of an equilateral triangle. If the area of the equilateral triangle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math>&nbsp;sq. units, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "48",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0023_3bdc6399c074.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.06667in;height:1.47986in\" /></p><p>From the diagram,</p><p><math><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math></p>"
  }
